%TAG !u! tag:unity3d.com,2011:
--- !u!114 &11400000
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 72a2054a7b2ea8346b8e03ab6c5935fc, type: 3}
  m_Name: Handbook
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::LostControl.Config.HandbookContent
  pages:
  - title: Basics
    body: '<b>Your job</b>

      Users send a ticket when their PC has a problem.
      Fix every PC before too many users are lost.


      <b>Connecting</b>

      Click
      a ticket in the list to connect to that PC. Connecting takes a few seconds,
      and you can only work on one PC at a time. Disconnect with the button above
      the list.


      <b>The list goes stale</b>

      While you are connecting
      or connected, the other tickets stop updating: they are dimmed and only show
      what you last saw. When a PC you can''t see takes damage, you hear a beep and
      its ticket flashes red. Disconnect to see every ticket live again.


      <b>Rounds</b>

      Each
      PC is fixed by finishing its minigame a few times. The list and the minigame
      panel show which round you are on. Finished rounds stay finished when you leave.


      <b>Pressure</b>

      While
      a round is unsolved, the PC''s pressure meter fills, also while you are working
      on another PC. When it is full, the PC takes damage and the meter drops back
      to half. Finishing a round empties it.


      <b>Damage</b>

      Fine, Slightly
      broken, More broken, Blackout. At Blackout the user is lost and the ticket
      closes. The level ends when every ticket is closed, or when too many users
      are lost (see Game data).'
  - title: Find the off-folder
    body: 'One folder in the grid looks slightly different from the others. Click
      it to finish the round.


      <b>What can be different</b>

      The file
      on the folder, the side of the tab, the colour (a little lighter or darker),
      a small tilt, or the size. In each round only one of these is different.


      <b>Careful</b>

      Clicking
      a folder that is not the different one adds pressure.


      <b>Pressure</b>

      The
      meter fills at a steady speed while the round is unsolved.'
